# Explicit, not inherited. Vercel falls back to .gitignore only when this
# file is absent, and 59GB of brand library, retreat photography and video
# now sit inside this folder. Not worth relying on a fallback for.
CydnieJocelyn-Site/
Costa Rica copy/
Family Travel copy/
Fonts copy/
cydniejocelyn/

.git/
.DS_Store
# Local Claude tooling. `launch.json` holds absolute paths to a preview
# server on this machine, and until 28 August 2026 build.py walked into this
# folder and copied it into dist/, so it was uploaded on every deploy and
# served at /.claude/launch.json. Excluded here AND in build.py's
# EXCLUDE_DIRS; the drift check at the bottom of build.py keeps the two lists
# honest with each other.
.claude/

# TOOLS/ IS NOT EXCLUDED ANY MORE, AND IT CANNOT BE. `vercel.json` now runs
# `python3 tools/build.py` as the buildCommand, so excluding this folder
# removes the very file the build runs: the first deploy after that change
# failed in 0ms for exactly this reason. It is safe to upload now in a way it
# was not before, because `outputDirectory` is `dist` and Vercel serves only
# what is inside it. Nothing in tools/ is reachable over the wire.
#
# Everything else here is still working documents, not build inputs.
HANDOFF.md
BRIEF.md
README.md
# Added 31 August 2026, the same hour the file was created. Without it the
# build copied it into dist/ and it would have been served at /CLAUDE.md:
# working notes, the deploy mechanics and the list of what the brand refuses,
# public. Caught by looking in dist/ before pushing, not by any check.
CLAUDE.md
# Found live and crawlable on 14 September 2026: the home restructure brief,
# with the phase plan and the Gatlinburg launch date in it.
home-restructure-claude-code-brief.md

# Working documents. These are wireframes, briefs and copy decks that arrive
# as folders beside the site, and Vercel serves whatever it is given: the
# build brief was live at /The Build page/files/CLAUDE-CODE-BRIEF.md and
# returning 200 to anyone who guessed the path. Add the folder here the same
# day a new one lands, and never park a working document inside a route
# directory like the-build/.
The Build page/
Greece Retreat/
# Renamed from `Retreats/`. A draft folder whose name differs from a route
# directory only by case is a trap: this project is uploaded from a
# case-insensitive filesystem, so `Retreats/` here could have taken the
# real `/retreats/` page out of the deploy with it.
Retreat drafts/
# Both arrived mid-session on 26 August 2026 and were built on 26 August into
# /a-sounding/ and /the-letters/. The wireframes stay excluded: they carry an
# annotation layer, a notes toggle and, in the Letters draft, a live HoneyBook
# widget pointed at the retired Collective form.
#
# Checked against the case-insensitive-filesystem trap above: lowercased,
# `a sounding` and `the letters page` are neither of them `a-sounding` or
# `the-letters`, so neither draft can take a route directory out of the
# deploy with it. Keep it that way when renaming either.
A Sounding/
The Letters Page/
# Arrived 26 August 2026, 19:07. Built on 28 August into /thequestions/.
# The wireframe stays excluded: it carries an annotation layer and three
# copy variants that are not the ones that shipped.
#
# Checked against the case-insensitive-filesystem trap above: lowercased,
# `the questions` is not `thequestions`, so the draft cannot take the route
# directory out of the deploy with it. Keep it that way when renaming.
the questions/
# Arrived 26 August 2026, later the same evening. Built on 28 August into
# /privacy-policy/, which closes the cutover trap in HANDOFF section 7.3.
# The deck stays excluded: it carries four FLAG lines addressed to Cydnie,
# and a document that argues with itself in the margins is not the document
# people should be reading when they look up what they signed.
Privacy terms page/
# Arrived 30 August 2026, 19:37, while a session was running: 48 location
# screenshots, 145MB, for a Gatlinburg retreat that is on no page. Excluded
# the same day it landed, per the rule above. Two reasons and either is
# enough: 145MB of upload on every deploy, and these are unreleased location
# photographs for an event that has not been announced.
April Retreat Gatlinburg April 13th - 18th /
# Arrived 21 September 2026 for the May 2027 retreat, which is prelaunch and
# on no public page. Same two reasons as the folder above.
May Retreat Arizona May 5th - 9th/

# Referenced by nothing. Moved here out of assets/img/ on 28 August rather
# than deleted, because most of them are alternates of files that are still
# in use. See assets/_unused/README.md. `tools/build.py` warns if assets/img/
# grows another one.
assets/_unused/

# THE BACKEND SECRETS AND THE LOCAL ENVIRONMENT.
# `.env.local` holds three database passwords and the IP hashing salt. It is
# gitignored, so it would never reach Vercel through git, but `vercel deploy`
# from this machine uploads the working directory and would carry it. The
# real values belong in the project's environment variables, not in a file.
#
# `.venv` is 777 files of built wheels. Vercel installs from requirements.txt.
#
.env
.env.local
.env.example
.venv/
__pycache__/

# `api/` IS LISTED, AND THAT IS THE SWITCH.
#
# Vercel turns every file in api/ into a live serverless function the moment
# it is uploaded. On this repo a push is a deploy, so committing api/ without
# this line would put four public write endpoints on cydniejocelyn.com the
# same minute, and nothing on the site calls them. An endpoint nobody uses is
# still an endpoint somebody can find: spam, rows, and a bill, for no benefit.
#
# The database and the code are kept because they are wanted later. They are
# kept SWITCHED OFF because "later" is not today.
#
# DELETING THE NEXT LINE IS WHAT MAKES THEM LIVE. Before doing it: confirm
# SITE_DATABASE_URL and IP_SALT are set in the Vercel project, and have a
# page that actually calls an endpoint, or you have opened a door onto an
# empty room. See HANDOFF section 51.
api/
